    <statement><p>Find the integral</p>
<p><m>\int\,y\root 5\of{y + 1}\,dy =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.833333y\mathopen{}\left(y+1\right)^{1.2}-0.378788\mathopen{}\left(y+1\right)^{2.2}+C</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\int\,u\,v'\,dx = u\cdot v - \int u'\,v\,dx</m>)
with <m>u = y</m> and <m>v' = (y +
1)^{1/5}</m>.  Then <m>u' = 1</m> and <m>v = {5\over
6}(y+1)^{6/5}</m>.  Thus
<me>\int\,y (y + 1)^{1/5}\,dy = 
    ({5\over 6})\cdot y\cdot (y+1)^{6/5} - 
    \int\,{5\over 6}(y + 1)^{6/5}\,dy =</me>
<me>({5\over 6})\cdot y\cdot (y+1)^{6/5} - 
      {25\over 66}\cdot(y + 1)^{11/5} + C.</me>



</solution>
